# Feature Module Patterns

## Adding or changing a feature

Follow this order; each step must compile:

1. `domain/` — types, enums, pure functions
2. `validation.ts` — Zod schemas (`ObjectIdSchema` for Mongo IDs)
3. `src/models/` — Mongoose schema (import sub-schemas from domain when possible)
4. `services/` — one file per action (`create.ts`, `update.ts`, `list.ts`)
5. `services/index.ts` — re-export public services only
6. `src/app/api/...` — thin route handlers
7. `ui/` — components; pages in `src/app/(dashboard)/`

## Service conventions

```typescript
// ✅ Service pattern
export async function createThing(input: unknown) {
  await connectMongo();
  const data = CreateThingSchema.parse(input);
  // validate business rules, then persist
  return mapThingDetails(doc);
}
```

- Call `connectMongo()` at the start of async services
- Parse input with Zod in the service (not only in the route)
- Map Mongoose documents to plain objects before returning to API/UI
- Put multi-step builders in `services/internal/`

## UI conventions

- `"use client"` only when hooks or browser APIs are needed
- Forms: react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod`
- Fetch via API routes from client components; server pages call services directly
- Keep wizard/stepper state in the page or top-level component, not in domain

## Avoid

- Business logic in UI components or API route files
- Exporting `services/internal/` helpers from the feature barrel
- Duplicating Zod schemas between validation.ts and inline in components
